      {
        "id": 19396,
        "name": "felipejoker",
        "username": "felipejoker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/felipejoker/{size}/2075_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-09-01T02:51:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Greetings, first time posting, hope this is ok.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>So, I intend to GM SCRPG when its finally ready, but a friend of mine got so excited that he wanted to make a character right away, just to feel how the game plays.<br>\n<br>\nWe got into 2 problems:</p>\n<p>Frist one being that he wanted to make a character that would jump in front of danger to save others - someone with high mobility and density/body-morphing so he could become rubber or elastic-like.</p>\n<p>So he got a bunch of powers to reduce the damage he takes/ improving his defense.<br>\n<br>\nAnd got \"Misdirection\", so he could save others.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nWhat is the problem? Its that they don't work well together, it seems: \"misdirection\" cancels the attack and transfers the leftover damage to another target. BUT - if you have damage reduction, you would redirect less damage... The same would be valid if he had boosted himself before the defense:&nbsp; the leftover damage would be minimized... And that does not make much sense to me. Can someone help me understand the Idea, or suggest another ability that may serve better for this pourpose?&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nThank you in advance.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:03.832Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 30,
        "reads": 2,
        "readers_count": 1,
        "score": 150.4,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19394,
        "topic_slug": "how-does-misdirection-ability-work-from-experimentation-power-source",
        "display_username": "felipejoker",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
